# Trivy ignore list — findings that have been triaged.
#
# Every CVE here must reference an open `SD-*` row in docs/AUDIT_DEBT.md or
# a documented runtime decision. When a CVE is fixed in the lockfile, drop
# its row from this file so the Trivy gate can detect regressions.

# SD-15: @octokit/{plugin-paginate-rest,request,request-error} bumped via
# pnpm.overrides created a transitive break — newer plugin/request versions
# require @octokit/core >=5, but `@octokit/rest@19.0.13` (used by
# `backend/src/shared/github-service.ts` for bug-report integration) ships
# @octokit/core@4.2.4. Bumping `@octokit/rest` to v22 also requires bumping
# `@octokit/auth-app` 6→8 (a runtime auth flow change) — out of scope for
# this PR. Suppressing the three MEDIUM CVEs in Code Scanning until the
# @octokit lineage is migrated as a separate workstream.
CVE-2025-25288
CVE-2025-25289
CVE-2025-25290

# SD-15: vite 5→8 + esbuild bumps blocked by vite 8's switch to Rolldown,
# which deprecates the `manualChunks: object` rollup API used in
# `admin-panel/vite.config.ts` and `vendor-panel/vite.config.ts`, plus
# `@vitejs/plugin-react@4.x` does not officially support vite 8 (peer dep
# capped at vite 6). Fixing requires rewriting both vite configs to use
# `manualChunks` as a function and bumping the React plugin — beyond the
# scope of this dep-cleanup PR. Suppressing the two MEDIUM CVEs until the
# Rolldown migration is tackled as a separate workstream.
CVE-2026-39365
GHSA-67mh-4wv8-2f99
